---
description: >-
  `swimlane.ignoreCrossLaneEdges: false`: cross-lane edges count when ranks
  are assigned (gravity layering, then `optimizeRanksByCrossings`, which
  acts only then, as in v12), so Shop's and Courier's steps line up after
  the Customer steps that lead to them. With the default (`true`) each lane
  is ranked on its own edges and compacted.
config:
  swimlane:
    ignoreCrossLaneEdges: false
---
swimlane-beta TB
  subgraph Customer
    A[Order] --> B[Pay]
    B --> C[Receive]
  end
  subgraph Shop
    D[Pick] --> E[Pack]
  end
  subgraph Courier
    F[Collect] --> G[Deliver]
  end
  A --> D
  E --> F
  G --> C
  B --> E
